# Windows shells need CRLF. A .cmd file with bare newlines is mis-parsed by
# cmd.exe, and the symptom is obscure: the last token on a line gets run as a
# command of its own, which is where "'*' is not recognized" came from.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
